# HTML Email Design (ALL outbound mail)

Every email APICS sends (registration, status, notifications, reminders, admin alerts) must look like a **modern, professional Philippine LGU / OCBO** message — not a bare Markdown dump, plain `nl2br` body, or browser-default page.

Applies to: `app/Mail/**`, `resources/views/emails/**`, and any future Mailable.

## Mandatory layout

1. **Shared shell** — Always extend `emails.layouts.apics` (or a child of it). Do **not** invent one-off full HTML documents per Mailable.
2. **Letterhead band**
   - CSFP seal (`asset('images/branding/csfp-seal.png')` as absolute URL)
   - LGU line: City of San Fernando, Pampanga · OCBO
   - System line: APICS (Automated Permitting, Inspection, and Compliance System)
3. **Document identity**
   - Clear headline + optional eyebrow (e.g. Registration · Approved)
   - Preheader text (hidden preview line for inbox clients)
4. **Structured body**
   - Short greeting, 1–3 short paragraphs, optional meta panel (label/value rows)
   - Primary CTA as a **table-based button** (`emails.partials.button`) — never raw `<a>` styled only with Tailwind/utility classes
   - Secondary link as plain URL under the button when useful (email clients strip fancy CSS)
5. **Footer**
   - Office name, system-generated notice, optional contact from `config('apics_public')`
   - No Velzon chrome, no app sidebar, no interactive JS

## Design & brand

- Colors: civic navy `#0F172A`, brand red `#FF2222` for primary CTA only, slate text `#334155` / muted `#64748B`, white card on `#F1F5F9` canvas
- Typography: system stack (`-apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif`) — no web-font `@import` (blocked by many clients)
- Card: max-width **600px**, centered, soft border, generous padding
- Avoid purple gradients, dark-mode-only themes, and decorative clutter

## Mobile & multi-client (required)

Email clients are not browsers. Optimize for **Gmail, Apple Mail (iOS/macOS), Outlook, Yahoo, Samsung Mail**:

| Requirement | Rule |
|-------------|------|
| Layout | Nested `<table role="presentation">` — **no** flexbox/grid as primary layout |
| CSS | Prefer **inline** styles on elements; put `@media` only in `<style>` in the head |
| Width | Fluid wrapper; inner content ≤ 600px; stack columns under ~620px |
| Images | Absolute `https`/`APP_URL` URLs; `alt` text; `display:block`; width constrained |
| Touch | CTA min height ~44px; full-width button on small screens |
| Dark mode | Provide `@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark)` overrides where practical; keep contrast readable |
| Plain text | Ship a matching `text` view (or `->text()`) alongside HTML |
| Escape | Always `{{ }}` / `e()` — never inject raw user HTML into email bodies |

## Implementation rules

- Mailables use `Content(html: 'emails…', text: 'emails…-text', with: […])` — not bare `htmlString` for product mail
- Reuse partials: `emails.partials.header`, `footer`, `button`, `panel`, `meta-row`
- Absolute links via `url()` / `config('app.url')` — relative paths break in clients
- Respect `MAIL_ENABLED` / `MailSender` — do not bypass the mail gate
- No tracking scripts, no external CSS files, no `<script>`

## Anti-patterns

```text
❌ Laravel default Markdown shell as the final product look
❌ htmlString / nl2br-only notification bodies for user-facing mail
❌ Tailwind classes / Vite CSS (clients strip them)
❌ Flex/grid-only layouts; hover-only CTAs
❌ Missing preheader, letterhead, or plain-text alternative
❌ Oversized images, unescaped user content, relative asset URLs
```

## Checklist before saying done

- [ ] Extends `emails.layouts.apics` (or shared child)
- [ ] Letterhead + headline + preheader present
- [ ] CTA uses table button partial; readable without CSS
- [ ] Looks usable at ~320–414px width and on desktop
- [ ] Plain-text sibling included
- [ ] Dynamic values escaped; absolute URLs for images/links
